#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# attributes

#% text
# `attributes(f)` gives the list of the attributes of the symbol `f`: `listable`, `hold_all`, `hold_first`, `hold_rest`, `orderless`, `effect`, `handles_failures`, `protected`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is held: `attributes(f)` names the symbol `f`, whatever value it has.

#% item
# `orderless` stands for an associative and commutative head (arguments flattened and sorted).

#% item
# `protected` (given by `protect`): the symbol's definitions may not change.

#% item
# `constant` marks a mathematical constant; the built-in constants (`pi`, `e`, `degree`, `euler_gamma`, `catalan`, `glaisher`, `khinchin`, `golden_ratio`, `golden_angle`, `champernowne_number`, `machine_precision`) have it. It changes no evaluation.

#% item
# A string names the symbol of that name, as `names` gives them: `attributes("pi")`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
attributes(add)
#% output
#= [flat, listable, orderless]

#% cell
attributes(table)
#% output
#= [hold_all]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `set_attributes` gives a symbol attributes:

#% cell
set_attributes(g1, listable)
attributes(g1)
#% output
#= [listable]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `set_attributes`, `clear_attributes`
